* Senior Data Engineer

C2H / FTE  
Work Location – Bangalore, Pune, Kolkata and Indore  
Budget – 30 LPA  
Interview process – 1st Online assessment F2F & After that technical round, 2nd Virtual Technical round  
JD :-  
What We're Looking For...

* Master's degree or foreign equivalent in Information Systems, Data Science, Data Analytics, Computer Science, Computer Engineering, or related field.
* Five (5) years of work experience in the position offered, as a Data Engineer, Software Developer, or related occupation.
* Must have experience with the following:

o Working in a production data environment, with responsibility for building, maintaining, and supporting data pipelines and platforms;  
o Leading cloud data migrations and platform modernization efforts, including planning, execution, and support of production systems during and after migration;  
o BigQuery, Snowflake, and cloud-based data architectures, including designing, optimizing, and operating scalable data solutions in cloud environments; o Migrating, supporting, and maintaining BI and reporting platforms such as Looker (Mode experience), including ensuring data accuracy, performance, and reliability of reporting;  
o SQL (Structured Query Language) and Python, with demonstrated ability to troubleshoot and resolve complex data quality, performance, and integration issues;  
o Working with ETL/ELT (Extract, Transform, Load) tools (Talend) and modern data pipeline patterns, including data ingestion, transformation, orchestration, and monitoring in production environments;  
o Building and managing marketing data integrations, including integrations with search engines, social media platforms, and other third-party marketing data sources;  
o Internal and external API (Application Programming Interface) integrations, including ingesting, validating, and maintaining data from third-party and internal systems;  
o Data warehousing concepts, including dimensional modeling, performance optimization, and cost aware design in cloud data platforms;  
o Own and deliver complex technical solutions end-to-end (design, implementation, and support) using distributed systems, cloud platforms (one of the following: AWS (Amazon Web Services), GCP (Google Cloud Platform), Azure), data frameworks (one of the following: Spark, Kafka), and programing languages (one of the following: Python, C#, SQL), while prioritizing effectively and balancing speed, quality, and long-term goals; o Work independently while collaborating cross-functionally (engineering, analytics, product, and business), using tools such as Git, Jira, and BI platforms (one of the following: Tableau, Looker, Power BI), and proactively managing workstreams and contributing to team standards;

Pay: ₹1,500,000.00 - ₹250,000,000.00 per year

Benefits:

* Flexible schedule
* Provident Fund

Work Location: Hybrid remote in Bangalore City, Bengaluru, Karnataka
